EXT. FROZEN LAKE - ICE-FISHING HUT - NIGHT

A tin shack on the ice, a single yellow window. Snow drifts in the dark. A string of lights marks a path back to the shore, now very far away.

INT. ICE-FISHING HUT - CONTINUOUS

Cramped. A propane heater. Two folding stools. A round hole in the floor shows black water under a skin of ice.

WILHELMINA BRODERICK-ADEYEMI (60s, wool cap, flask) sits on one stool, holding a rod. Her grandson FELIX (12, puffy coat, wide eyes) sits on the other, watching the hole.

She tugs the line. Nothing.

FELIX
Grandma.

WILHELMINA
Patience.

FELIX
It's been an hour.

WILHELMINA
The fish don't know that.

He sighs. Rubs his hands over the heater.

FELIX
Can I tell you something?

WILHELMINA
Always.

FELIX
I like it here.

WILHELMINA
Good boy.

She smiles. Sips from the flask. Then frowns.

The line twitches. She reels slowly. A tug, hard. She leans back, braces.

WILHELMINA (CONT'D)
Get the net.

He grabs it. Kneels by the hole.

The line goes slack. Wilhelmina pulls it up. The hook is bare, clean, polished.

WILHELMINA (CONT'D)
Huh.

FELIX
Did we lose it?

WILHELMINA
We did.

She re-baits. Drops the line. They wait.

The heater ticks. Wind presses the shack. Through the hole, the black water seems to ripple, but there is no wind below the ice.

FELIX
Grandma.

WILHELMINA
Shh.

FELIX
Something's under us.

She lifts her head. Sees it too. A paleness rises in the water. A shape. Round. Broad. Slowly turning.

WILHELMINA
(very softly)
Felix. Back up.

He doesn't move. He's staring.

FELIX
It has a face.

She drops the rod, seizes him by the coat, and drags him away from the hole. The pale thing breaks the surface. It is not a fish. It is not anything. Two white hands grip the edge of the ice and pull, and the water around them runs black and silent.

WILHELMINA
Out! The door!

She pushes him. He fumbles with the latch. The thing hauls itself into the hut, dripping, long-limbed, tilting its head to one side, looking at them both with an expression of mild and infinite hunger. The heater gutters and goes out.
